<Wiki
  title="puv create"
  description="Fetch a Laravel, CodeIgniter, Symfony, or Slim skeleton and import its composer.json."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>create</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv create</code> fetches an application skeleton. <code>puv init</code> starts an empty
    project. <code>create</code> starts from a named template.
  </p>

  <h2>Named templates</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv create laravel blog
puv create codeigniter
puv create symfony
puv create slim</pre>
  <p>
    The first argument is the template. <code>puv create laravel blog</code> fetches the Laravel
    skeleton into <code>blog</code>. <code>codeigniter</code>, <code>symfony</code>, and
    <code>slim</code> are the other template names.
  </p>

  <h2>No name</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv create</pre>
  <p>
    In a terminal, <code>puv create</code> with no template asks which template to use.
  </p>

  <h2>Composer files in the skeleton</h2>
  <p>
    A <code>composer.json</code> in the skeleton is imported with
    <a href="/wiki/commands/contain"><code>contain</code></a>. What that import keeps, copies,
    and skips is that page. Installing the resulting lock is
    <a href="/wiki/commands/sync"><code>puv sync</code></a>.
  </p>
</Wiki>
